<title>UK: UK new construction orders down in 3mths to July.</title>
<headline>UK new construction orders down in 3mths to July.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.K. new construction orders were 5.0 percent lower in the three months to July versus the previous three months but were up by 2.0 percent on the same period in 1995, the Department of the Environment said.  </p>
<p>			  3/mth vs 3/mth    3/mth vs same 95</p>
<p> Total			 -5.0		    +2.0</p>
<p> Private Housing	   -18.0		   -12.0</p>
<p> Public Housing	    -25.0		   -27.0</p>
<p> Infrastructure	    -16.0		   +26.0</p>
<p> Public non-housing	-4.0		    -22.0</p>
<p> Private industrial	-6.0		     UNCH</p>
<p> Private commercial	+21.0		    +22.0</p>
<p>In current prices the total value of new orders in July alone was 1.898 billion stg. (All table figures in percent)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom ++44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
